  "_doc": "THE WORDS READERS ACTUALLY TYPE (2026-08-01, W2.5d). Search vocabulary only — these are NOT clinical claims, and nothing here is rendered to a reader as content. build/parse.js folds them into p.solveAlias (a de-duplicated word bag) and p.solvePhrases (whole phrases), which site/app.js rankProblems() and server.js searchSolve() both read, so the two runtimes stay identical. WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: measured against the shipped index, 9 of a 20-query battery of realistic phrasings ranked the wrong problem #1 — 'hair falling out' returned insomnia, because insomnia's display name is 'Trouble Falling Asleep' and 'falling' is a NAME word worth 18; 'lose weight' returned pcos as its ONLY hit, because 'PCOS / Hormonal Weight' owns the word 'weight' and fat-loss-plateau's name and hay contain it nowhere; 'balding' returned nothing at all. The corpus is authored in clinical language and readers type symptoms. RULE FOR EDITING: only add a phrase a reader would plausibly type for THAT problem. Never add a phrase to make a query rank — if a query is ambiguous between two problems, both may claim it, and the ranking will show both. GATES: build/parse.js fails the build on an unknown problem id, a problem with no entry, an empty list or an empty phrase; scripts/smoke.mjs (solveBattery) fails on a 20-query regression battery run against the live server, plus the invariant that all 41 problems rank #1 for their own display name. Measured: without this file the battery scores 11/20, with it 20/20.",
